# Contributing to {{project_name}}

## Setup

```bash
make setup
pre-commit install   # format, lint and secret scan on every commit
make check
```

## Workflow

1. Create a branch from `main`: `feat/short-description`, `fix/...`, `docs/...`.
2. Keep the change small and focused. One concern per PR.
3. Add or update tests for every behaviour change.
4. Run `make check` locally — it is exactly what CI runs.
5. Open a PR using the template. CI must be green and one approval is required.
6. Squash-merge. The squash commit message follows Conventional Commits.

## Commit messages — Conventional Commits

```
feat: add VIP discount to checkout
fix(order): prevent double charge on retry
docs: explain points rule in glossary
refactor | test | chore | ci | perf: ...
```

`feat` and `fix` drive automatic versioning and the CHANGELOG. Use `feat!:` or
a `BREAKING CHANGE:` footer for breaking changes.

## Domain changes

If you add or change a business concept or rule, update `ontology/` in the same PR
and mention it in the PR description — ontology changes need a reviewer who knows the domain.

## Decisions and incidents

Record significant decisions in `wiki/decisions/` and production incidents in
`wiki/incidents/` (formats in `ontology/page-types.yaml`).
